// ── Common Drugs & Pharmacology · cases
const NEURO_MED_CASES_RECALL: RecallQ[] = [
  { id: 1, question: "CASE: You suspect Horner syndrome on the right. Describe the pharmacologic work-up and what each result means.", answer: "CONFIRM: apraclonidine 0.5–1% (the denervation-supersensitive Horner pupil DILATES, reversing the anisocoria) or cocaine 4–10% (Horner pupil fails to dilate). LOCALIZE: hydroxyamphetamine 1% — if the Horner pupil fails to dilate, the lesion is THIRD-order (postganglionic); if it dilates, it is first/second-order. NEXT STEP: image by order and acuity (acute painful → carotid dissection)." },
  { id: 2, question: "CASE: A dilated pupil is suspected to be a tonic (Adie) pupil versus pharmacologic blockade. How do you use pilocarpine to decide?", answer: "DILUTE pilocarpine 0.1% constricts a tonic (Adie) pupil (denervation supersensitivity) but not a normal pupil. Pilocarpine 1% constricts a CN III-palsy pupil (intact receptors) but a pharmacologically (atropine-) blocked pupil will NOT constrict even to 1%. NEXT STEP: history of drops/plants; reassure if Adie." },
  { id: 3, question: "CASE: A TB patient on ethambutol develops bilateral painless vision loss, dyschromatopsia, and cecocentral scotomas at ~2 months. Work through the approach.", answer: "LOCALIZE: a toxic optic neuropathy (papillomacular bundle). DIFFERENTIAL: ethambutol toxicity (dose-related >25 mg/kg/day), other toxins/nutritional. INVESTIGATIONS: colour vision, fields, document the drug/dose. NEXT STEP: STOP ethambutol (may be permanent); monitor recovery." },
  { id: 4, question: "CASE: A young obese woman with IIH needs medical therapy. What do you give and what do you watch for?", answer: "FIRST-LINE: weight loss plus acetazolamide (a carbonic anhydrase inhibitor that lowers CSF production; proven in the IIHTT). Watch for paresthesias, metallic taste, kidney stones, hypokalemia, and sulfa allergy. Topiramate is an alternative that also aids weight loss (good with migraine). NEXT STEP: optic nerve sheath fenestration/shunt if vision is threatened." },
];
